---
title: "Introduction to Sociology"
code: "SOC-200"
category: "sociology"
credits: "3"
prerequisites: []
corequisites: []
---

Introduces the fundamental concepts and principles of sociology with attention to sociological theory, research methods, and the impact of social inequality. Examines a variety of topics such as culture, race, social class, gender, major social institutions and their role in contemporary society, and the processes of social change. Lecture 3 hours per week.
